[h1]Military Drop - Radio Supply Airdrops[/h1]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/banner.png[/img]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer · Standalone[/b]

[i]Multiplayer: the mod is built for dedicated servers (the server decides everything), but it has only been tested in singleplayer so far. Please report any multiplayer issue.[/i]

Tune a military radio to the right frequency, give this week's code and requisition military supplies. A helicopter drops a crate far away and announces the grid to everyone listening... and the noise draws the dead.

[b]BREAKING CHANGE — 0.1.2:[/b] Reputation belongs to each character. Old collective scores were not transferred: existing characters start at 25.

[h2]Find the frequency and the code[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-code.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/codebook-memo.png[/img]

Military and police memos reveal the frequency. Every Monday, decipher the shortwave numbers broadcast with the military codebook.

[h2]Call from your radio[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-radio.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/walkie-logistics.png[/img]

Right-click a military radio, [b]Device Options[/b], [b]Logistics[/b] section: type the code and press [b]Request a supply drop[/b]. Walkie-talkie in hand, on the belt or in a bag, or a placed radio.

[h2]Fill the requisition[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-requisition.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/requisition-form.png[/img]

Choose from 18 loot-table lots, mods included, within your point budget. Or request a siren decoy to draw hordes away.

[h2]Reach the crate[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-crate.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/crate-trunk.png[/img]

Reach the grid 150–400 tiles away; a horde guards the crate. Empty crates can be dismantled for wood.

[b]Keep a radio on the military frequency.[/b] The grid and map marker arrive at landing and every 6 h until a case is opened. Off or on another channel: no announcement or marker. Save the frequency with [b]Add preset[/b].

[h2]When a helicopter goes down[/h2]

A supply helicopter can crash, more often in storms. Its MAYDAY gives a sector on the military frequency. At the wreck, the pilot carries a memo, a codebook and the [b]flight recorder[/b]; strip the wreck for parts, then cut it up. The order is lost with it, unless the server says otherwise.

[h2]Earn the base's trust[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-trust.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/console-missions.png[/img]

Personal trust shortens the wait and unlocks bigger requisitions. A new character starts at 25; saving, reconnecting or changing factions keeps their score.

[h3]Reputation: gains and losses[/h3]

Drop changes apply only to the requesting character; a different opener gets 0. Other rewards go to the acting character. Times are game time; values are defaults.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Cause[/b][/td][td][b]Change[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Requester opens first case[/td][td]+10[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Another member of the calling faction opens first case[/td][td]+5[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Outsider opens first case[/td][td]−5[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]No case opened within 48 h of delivery[/td][td]−10[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Flight recorder read and sent, once per crash site, no cap[/td][td]+10[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]First daily situation report[/td][td]+1[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Each valid, unused named dog tag[/td][td]+2[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]First recon confirmation within 25 tiles / 48 h[/td][td]+3[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Most kills in clearance horde, 90% dead[/td][td]+5[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Radio check answered within 4 h, once per character[/td][td]+1[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]3 wrong codes / wrong-frequency calls in 1 h[/td][td]−2[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Optional erosion after 24 h without contact[/td][td]−1 / +1[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Daily cap: +8 per character, excluding drops. Liaison post bonus: report +2, tag +3, recon +5, radio check +2; clearance stays +5. Scores: 0–100; a loss below 15 cuts the line for 3 days. Expired missions, admin drops and decoys: 0. Erosion is off by default and moves the score toward 25.

[h2]Hold a liaison post[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/art-post.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/console.png[/img]

A fixed military ham radio becomes a shared station console: tasks to handle (flight recorders, dog tags), orders, log and drops. Its reading bay reads a flight recorder in 10 minutes before you send it to the base. Each faction has a call sign; standing is personal.

[h2]Contested drop zones (PvP)[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/zones-add.png[/img]

On PvP servers, the admin picks where crates fall: zones grouped into sectors (a park, a mall, flats in Louisville). Each drop takes the nearest or a random sector, then a zone by weight: nobody can camp the spot. The announcement names it ("LZ Central Park, grid..."); players can optionally choose the sector in the form, decoy included. The crate never lands in water, inside a building, in a non-PvP zone or a safehouse.

Admin panel in game ([b]Military Drop Zones[/b]): draw zones with the mouse, set sector and weight, [b]Highlight[/b] them on the ground, edit, disable, teleport. Off by default.

[h2]For server admins[/h2]

[list]
[*]60 sandbox options, applied without restarting (except frequencies): wait between drops (one week by default, for the whole server), distance, horde, code mode, trust, missions, requisition, decoy, crashes, drop zones.
[*]Requisition lots can be edited, disabled or added in Zomboid/Lua/MilitaryDrop/requisition.txt.
[*]Server-authoritative multiplayer. Admins can force a drop, crash the next helicopter and launch missions from a military radio.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]No other mod required.
[*]Designed to coexist with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3672792485]HEF - Helicopter Event Framework[/url].
[*]With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811010882]Signal Smoke[/url], green smoke marks the crate.
[*]Works with Better Walkie Talkies: its push-to-talk, voice and battery rules are kept.
[*]Items from your weapon and item mods appear in the crates.
[/list]

